## 11. Counted resources, joint interfaces and nonduplication

**Resource statement 11.1 (ownership and representations).** The lower
contract has one old specimen, occupied live dimension three, one actual
common preparation, base and epoch, fixed supplied preparation reference,
aligned clock and common permission/controller descriptions. The source
generator has the actual history-specific $x,\beta,m,B$ and waveform;
these are latent source resources, never installed in the cut processor.
For the finite witnesses all programmes use rationals, $\pi$ and, in
(AC.13), one algebraic height, with finite symbolic descriptions.
Arbitrary real histories need not have finite effective descriptions.

The comparison class grants arbitrarily large independent memories,
ancillas, randomness, computation, ideal local processing and precision.
No increase in those source-independent resources repairs (AC.7),
(AC.26) or (AC.33). Accessible source-sensitive clock latches, receiver
entanglement shares, old logs, returned environments, installed parameters,
references, controller pointers and callbacks all belong jointly in the
assisted input if present. A register's source-independent marginal does
not excuse its joint correlations from that accounting.

In §10 the source-bound actuator/configuration is an additional resource
of unestablished acquisition, representation size and physical cost.
Its prescribed CP law is not a hardware upper bound. The live coin is one
classical bit; acceptance is another retained event. The specimen remains
in $V$ on live success. Every stopped branch additionally retains original
mode, exact first timestamp, stopped state, old archive, reference and
updates. No fixed finite-bit storage of that exact event is inferred.
Event Memory and Coarse Aliasing's same-event bounds remain applicable
under their own complete accessible-memory contract.

A positive joint-observer construction would have to supply the actual
inputs, not merely describe their statistics. It must retain source/epoch,
all old archives, clock/reference and calibration, permissions, controller,
all selectors and all external update inputs that affect the declared
future. In [Process Geometry][PG] this is the actual joint image
(PG.3400b-full), its compatible successor (PG.3400c), and the full
success/failure running relation (PG.3402-run-next). A common channel
failing the single request here cannot instantiate that interface for the
promised menu. This is a necessary consumer test, not a construction of
the whole image.

[Atlas Stable Core][ATLAS] Theorem 6.3 requires each view individually to
have the stable kernel and support executable responses, selectors and
updates. [Transport–Memory Completion][TM] §§2.9–2.12, 2.18 requires the
actual common coherent source/port, aligned acquired readings, known
nonzero amplitudes and known nonzero record overlap. Our mixtures, bits
and conditional actuator construct none of those ports or readings.
[EnvironmentRecords][ENV] and [PhaseRecordRecoveryCriterion][PRRC], with
their owning Scribes, concern specified joint records and matching
operations. [TypedFiniteViewKernel][TFVK] and [DynamicsDescent][DD], with
their owning Scribes, require complete existing steps/fibre conditions.
None acquires an omitted observation or permission.

